*** Settings ***
Documentation    Triggers [FID4590 - Fault signature for crash or failure] on RUs under test
...    and checks if faultSignature part of alarm response contains correct values.
...
...    Fault is generated by killing eventcollector (RU family < 8), start-syscon-with-user (RU family => 8) process on tester RU.
...
...    NOTE: User must import /testsuite/WMP/GVe/Wroclaw/AiFSiteS/resources/variables.robot in their testsuite!
...
...    Fault ID name according to NIDD: EFaultId_CrashOrFailureSignatureAl
...
...    Author:        dawid.bak@nokia.com
...    Maintainer:    Dawid Bak

Resource    ./FM_Fault_Signature.resource


*** Keywords ***
TC__FM_Fault_Signature_FID_4590
    [Documentation]
    ...  Triggers FID4590 and checks if faultSignature part of alarm response contains correct values
    ...
    ...  |  **Author:**      dawid.bak@nokia.com
    ...  |  **Maintainer:**  dawid.bak@nokia.com

  Common Test Setup
  Logging With Timestamp
    ...  message=RF Fault Signature FID4590
    ...  style=STEP
    ...  frame=${TRUE}

    ${rf_list}=    Get Dictionary Keys   ${cfg.RF_INFO}
    ${RF_status}=   Run Keyword And Return Status    Variable Should Exist    ${CUSTOM_RADIO_UNIT_LIST}
    ${rf_list}=    Set Variable If   ${RF_status}    ${CUSTOM_RADIO_UNIT_LIST}    ${rf_list}
    FOR   ${ru_sn}    IN    @{rf_list}
      ${ru_bts_id}    ${ru_dist_name}=    SITE Get RU Node Data    ${ru_sn}
      ${alarm_info}  ${ru_off_timestamp}=  Generate Radio Fault FID4590  ru_sn=${ru_sn}
      ...  connection=${ru_bts_id}
      FM Analyze Alarm List For Fault Signature  alarm_info=${alarm_info}
      ...  faultId=4590
      ...  fault_signature_scheme=${FID4590_FAULT_SIGNATURE_SCHEME}
      ...  alarm_details_scheme=${FID_4590_ALARM_INFO}
      ...  fault_signature_timestamp=${ru_off_timestamp}
      ...  ru_sn=${ru_sn}
      ...  connection=${ru_bts_id}
      ...  forbidden_severities=Critical
      ${ru_cell_affected_dict}=  SITE Create Affected Cells List RF Hot Remove Insert  ru_sn=${ru_sn}
      SITE Verify RU Affected Cells  bts_id=${ru_bts_id}
      ...  ru_cell_affected_dict=${ru_cell_affected_dict}
      ...  state=Insert
      ...  timeout=${RADIO_AVAILABILITY_TIMEOUT} sec
    END
    ${onair_status}=  Run Keyword And Ignore Error  STATE Verify Multi Node State  scf_check=${FALSE}  timeout=120
    IF  "${onair_status[0]}"=="FAIL"  Fail  BTS should be onair. Check states in logs.
    [Teardown]    Common Test Teardown

Generate Radio Fault FID4590
    [Arguments]  ${ru_sn}  ${connection}
    [Documentation]
    ...  Triggers FID4590 by terminating event collector process on tested radio.
    ...  After that check if radio resets and goes back online and if FID4590 is reported
    ...
    ...  |  **Author:**      dawid.bak@nokia.com
    ...  |  **Maintainer:**  dawid.bak@nokia.com
    ...
    ...  **Input Parameters:**
    ...
    ...  +--------------+------+--------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Parameter    | Man. | Description                                      |
    ...  +==============+======+==================================================+
    ...  | ru_sn        | Yes  | serial number of radio unit under test           |
    ...  +--------------+------+--------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | connection   | Yes  | alias for active ssh connection to SMOD          |
    ...  +--------------+------+--------------------------------------------------+
    ...
    ...  **Return parameters**
    ...
    ...  +------------------+--------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Parameter        | Description                                      |
    ...  +==================+==================================================+
    ...  | alarm_info       | list containing active alarms info               |
    ...  +------------------+--------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | ru_off_timestamp | timestam of the begining of the radio reset      |
    ...  +------------------+--------------------------------------------------+

    ${ru_bts_id}    ${ru_dist_name}=    SITE Get RU Node Data    ${ru_sn}
    ${ru_off_timestamp}=  Get Current Date  UTC
    Sleep  30  Timeout for fault signature timestamp
#    ${radio_family}=  radio.Get Radio Module Hardware Family  ru_name=${CFG['RF_INFO']['${ru_sn}']['scf_variant']}
#    ${process_name}=  Set Variable If  ${radio_family} >= 8  start-syscon-with-user   eventcollector
    radio.Kill Process On Radio Module By Name  ru_serial_number=${ru_sn}
    ...  process_name=eventcollector
    SITE Verify RU Power Remove Insert State  bts_id=${ru_bts_id}
    ...  dist_name=${ru_dist_name}
    ...  state=Remove
    ...  timeout=${FID_4590_TIMEOUT} sec
    SITE Verify RU Power Remove Insert State  bts_id=${ru_bts_id}
    ...  dist_name=${ru_dist_name}
    ...  state=Insert
    ...  timeout=${FID_4590_TIMEOUT} sec
    ${alarm_info}=  Assert Alarm Active  faultId=4590
    ...  faultName="Fault signature for crash or failure"
    ...  connection=${connection}  timeout=600
    Run Keyword And Ignore Error    admin.Add Allowed Alarm  faultId=4590  connection=${connection}
    Run Keyword And Ignore Error    admin.Add Allowed Alarm  faultId=10  connection=${connection}
    [Return]  ${alarm_info}  ${ru_off_timestamp}
